WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.266 --> 00:00:01.501
-Our next guest is
a very funny comedian and writer

00:00:01.501 --> 00:00:03.403 align:start size:94% position:6%
whose work you've seen on
"Desus and Mero,"

00:00:03.403 --> 00:00:05.672 size:88% position:44%
"Our Cartoon President,"
and "Yearly Departed."

00:00:05.672 --> 00:00:08.641 size:78% position:39%
Her new show, "Ziwe,"
premieres on Showtime

00:00:08.641 --> 00:00:09.876 size:78% position:39% line:92%
this Sunday, May 9th.

00:00:09.876 --> 00:00:10.643 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Let's take a look.

00:00:10.643 --> 00:00:12.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I'm honored
that you're doing the show

00:00:12.412 --> 00:00:16.082 align:start size:94% position:6%
But my question is
why did you agree to this?

00:00:16.082 --> 00:00:17.317 size:78% position:39% line:92%
Do you know who I am?

00:00:17.317 --> 00:00:19.486
-I don't have the slightest idea
who you are.

00:00:19.486 --> 00:00:22.055 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:22.055 --> 00:00:26.192
Someone who worked for you
was incredibly persistent,

00:00:26.192 --> 00:00:28.628 align:start size:94% position:6%
incredibly persistent
to the point

00:00:28.628 --> 00:00:29.462 line:92%
where this just seemed easier.

00:00:29.462 --> 00:00:32.799 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So, shout-out to the
persistence of women of color.

00:00:32.799 --> 00:00:35.802 align:start size:94% position:6%
Really.
-Yes, or any persistence.

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:40.774 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Please welcome to the sho
and the studio Ziwe!

00:00:40.774 --> 00:00:42.542 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:42.542 --> 00:00:43.543 align:start size:94% position:6%
Hello.
-Hi.

00:00:43.543 --> 00:00:45.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Welcome.
-Hi. Thanks for having me.

00:00:45.578 --> 00:00:46.946 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Everyone's so happy
you're here.

00:00:46.946 --> 00:00:50.216 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Hi, guys.
-Join us. Join us, Ziwe.

00:00:50.216 --> 00:00:52.485 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
♪♪♪♪

00:00:52.485 --> 00:00:53.653 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Hi. How are you?

00:00:53.653 --> 00:00:56.089 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Good. How are you?
-I am very well.

00:00:56.089 --> 00:00:59.759 align:start size:94% position:6%
I sort of became aware of
your work this year,

00:00:59.759 --> 00:01:01.061 line:92%
particularly on Instagram Live

00:01:01.061 --> 00:01:03.229 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was unaware
that we had met before.

00:01:03.229 --> 00:01:04.497 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Yes, we did.

00:01:04.497 --> 00:01:05.331 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-This was in 2013.

00:01:05.331 --> 00:01:08.201 align:start size:94% position:6%
We went -- We both went
to Northwestern University

00:01:08.201 --> 00:01:09.869 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes.
-And I went back for

00:01:09.869 --> 00:01:11.638 align:start size:94% position:6%
some sort of alumni event,
and there we are.

00:01:11.638 --> 00:01:15.341
-Yeah. You were trying to
avoid eye contact with me.

00:01:15.341 --> 00:01:17.777 size:81% position:41%
And I confronted you
into taking the photo.

00:01:17.777 --> 00:01:19.679 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Much like with Fran.
-Yes.

00:01:19.679 --> 00:01:21.448 align:start size:94% position:6%
I've been doing the same bit
for years.

00:01:21.448 --> 00:01:24.784 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And I was very touched becaus
you wrote "My writing hero

00:01:24.784 --> 00:01:27.353
in the tag and then I came
right back down to Earth

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:29.456 line:92%
because you misspelled my name

00:01:29.456 --> 00:01:32.459 align:start size:94% position:6%
You didn't --
-Okay, so, in my defense,

00:01:32.459 --> 00:01:35.962 align:start size:94% position:6%
autocorrect wasn't as poppin
on a BlackBerry Pearl.

00:01:35.962 --> 00:01:37.464 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh, yeah. That's true.
-So I'm sorry.

00:01:37.464 --> 00:01:39.232 align:start size:94% position:6%
-We're going to blame it
on the BlackBerry?

00:01:39.232 --> 00:01:39.933 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
I love your style.

00:01:39.933 --> 00:01:44.170 size:88% position:44%
You know, you've sort of
made a name for yourself

00:01:44.170 --> 00:01:45.605 line:92%
having very honest conversations

00:01:45.605 --> 00:01:46.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
about race
in a really funny way.

00:01:46.840 --> 00:01:48.808 align:start size:94% position:6%
Is that what we can expect
from the show as well?

00:01:48.808 --> 00:01:52.612 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes. It's going to be
a lot of really tense, silly

00:01:52.612 --> 00:01:55.648
bombastic conversations
with lots of music videos

00:01:55.648 --> 00:01:57.417 line:92%
and sketches and field pieces.

00:01:57.417 --> 00:01:59.319 line:92%
But it really is a wild time

00:01:59.319 --> 00:02:01.821
And you'll see interviews
you've never seen before.

00:02:01.821 --> 00:02:04.457 align:start size:94% position:6%
-So you took advantage of
Instagram Live

00:02:04.457 --> 00:02:06.526 align:start size:94% position:6%
during a time when a lot o
comedians, obviously,

00:02:06.526 --> 00:02:09.028 align:start size:94% position:6%
were suffering from not having
a room full of people

00:02:09.028 --> 00:02:10.396 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
to do their act to,

00:02:10.396 --> 00:02:14.000 align:start size:94% position:6%
and "Baited" was this way
to talk to people.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:15.768 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what made you use
this platform?

00:02:15.768 --> 00:02:18.471 align:start size:94% position:6%
And why do you think
people enjoyed it so much?

00:02:18.471 --> 00:02:19.506 size:88% position:44% line:92%
-Instagram Live? So I --

00:02:19.506 --> 00:02:22.509 align:start size:94% position:6%
At the height of the pandemic,
I had nothing to do.

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:23.209 size:88% position:44% line:92%
You couldn't go outside.

00:02:23.209 --> 00:02:25.211 align:start size:94% position:6%
I was afraid that if I wen
outside, I'd get COVID.

00:02:25.211 --> 00:02:29.949 align:start size:94% position:6%
And everyone was going liv
on Instagram every 15 minutes,

00:02:29.949 --> 00:02:34.354
and so I thought I would joi
that cacophony of notification

00:02:34.354 --> 00:02:35.221 line:92%
with my own type of show.

00:02:35.221 --> 00:02:37.891 align:start size:94% position:6%
But I was too lazy to do, like
a musical production.

00:02:37.891 --> 00:02:40.193 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I decided to do interviews,
which are kind of more --

00:02:40.193 --> 00:02:41.327 align:start size:94% position:6%
it's just -- I like
to talk to people.

00:02:41.327 --> 00:02:44.497 align:start size:94% position:6%
So what started off as, like
you know, this program

00:02:44.497 --> 00:02:47.400 align:start size:94% position:6%
with 30 viewers and, like,
very, very --

00:02:47.400 --> 00:02:51.070 size:81% position:41%
comedians who are just
my friends turned into

00:02:51.070 --> 00:02:53.973 align:start size:94% position:6%
I guess -- I don't know --
a phenomenon?

00:02:53.973 --> 00:02:56.409 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you -- what do you
say about yourself?

00:02:56.409 --> 00:02:59.412 align:start size:94% position:6%
-It certainly went from that
to a show on television.

00:02:59.412 --> 00:03:01.314 align:start size:94% position:6%
So I'm going to allow
phenomenon.

00:03:01.314 --> 00:03:03.082 line:92%
-Yeah, yeah. I mean, yes.

00:03:03.082 --> 00:03:03.983 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
Yeah, it's wild.

00:03:03.983 --> 00:03:05.718 align:start size:94% position:6%
One day, I book
Caroline Calloway.

00:03:05.718 --> 00:03:07.820 align:start size:94% position:6%
Then the next week,
I do Alison Roman.

00:03:07.820 --> 00:03:09.522 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then the next week,
I do Rose McGowan.

00:03:09.522 --> 00:03:10.924 align:start size:94% position:6%
And then, suddenly,
the show blew up.

00:03:10.924 --> 00:03:13.259 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And was it --
were you surprised that

00:03:13.259 --> 00:03:14.494 line:92%
you were starting to get guest

00:03:14.494 --> 00:03:16.362 align:start size:94% position:6%
with sort of bigger
and bigger name recognition?

00:03:16.362 --> 00:03:18.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
Or did it happen so quickl
that you didn't

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.266 align:start size:94% position:6%
even have time
to step back and say,

00:03:20.266 --> 00:03:22.001 size:75% position:38%
"Oh, I can't believe
this is happening"?

00:03:22.001 --> 00:03:23.336 line:92%
-Both because I come from

00:03:23.336 --> 00:03:24.737 align:start size:94% position:6%
a live performing background
in New York.

00:03:24.737 --> 00:03:28.041
I've been performing live to
very small audiences forever

00:03:28.041 --> 00:03:30.877 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I've become accustome
to DMing people,

00:03:30.877 --> 00:03:33.613 align:start size:94% position:6%
begging them to do my show
so yes.

00:03:33.613 --> 00:03:38.952 align:start size:94% position:6%
But the production behind it
was part of my skill set.

00:03:38.952 --> 00:03:40.553
-One of the things about
Instagram Live, of course,

00:03:40.553 --> 00:03:44.057
is you sort of can't block
anyone from coming to watch.

00:03:44.057 --> 00:03:46.626 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yeah, that's true.
-And I would assume you have

00:03:46.626 --> 00:03:47.994 line:92%
family members who realize

00:03:47.994 --> 00:03:49.862 align:start size:94% position:6%
there was this opportunity
to watch you.

00:03:49.862 --> 00:03:51.798 align:start size:94% position:6%
And what was their feedbac
on the show?

00:03:51.798 --> 00:03:54.500 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, so, my Nigerian aun
famously said that

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:58.037
I was very sweet but I needed to
be kinder to Democrats.

00:03:58.037 --> 00:03:59.239 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Oh.
-And I took those notes

00:03:59.239 --> 00:04:01.874 size:81% position:41%
with a grain of salt,
but also -- look, I --

00:04:01.874 --> 00:04:03.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
it allows me to reflect
on myself

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.445 align:start size:94% position:6%
because, hey, I should be nice
to Democrats.

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.447 align:start size:94% position:6%
-[ Laughs ]
That's very -- It's good.

00:04:07.447 --> 00:04:08.448 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-It's good advice.

00:04:08.448 --> 00:04:11.251 align:start size:94% position:6%
-I heard you tell
that somebody that you model

00:04:11.251 --> 00:04:14.854
your interviewing style afte
and that you're very inspired by

00:04:14.854 --> 00:04:17.991 size:75% position:38%
is Andy Cohen's work
with the Housewives.

00:04:17.991 --> 00:04:20.193 line:92%
-Yes. I'm a "Housewife" fanatic.

00:04:20.193 --> 00:04:22.095 align:start size:94% position:6%
I watch "Beverly Hills,"
"Auckland,"

00:04:22.095 --> 00:04:23.896 align:start size:94% position:6%
"Dallas," everything,
"Orange County."

00:04:23.896 --> 00:04:26.666
And I would watch these
interviews that -- the reunions,

00:04:26.666 --> 00:04:30.503
rather, that Andy would do wit
the characters, I call them.

00:04:30.503 --> 00:04:32.205 align:start size:94% position:6%
And he'd say,
"Hey, character, you know,

00:04:32.205 --> 00:04:35.675 align:start size:94% position:6%
Monique from New Jersey says
your boobs look awful."

00:04:35.675 --> 00:04:37.210 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they would have --
"What do you --

00:04:37.210 --> 00:04:38.578 align:start size:94% position:6%
What do you have
to say about that?"

00:04:38.578 --> 00:04:39.846 line:92%
And they'd have to answer.

00:04:39.846 --> 00:04:41.714 align:start size:94% position:6%
And they'd be put on the spo
and really tense

00:04:41.714 --> 00:04:44.417 align:start size:94% position:6%
but they'd still reveal that
about themselves.

00:04:44.417 --> 00:04:46.619 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so -- Or, like,
he'd confront, like,

00:04:46.619 --> 00:04:48.554 align:start size:94% position:6%
Camille Grammer
about her marriage.

00:04:48.554 --> 00:04:53.660 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I thought, "Why can I
not have -- I...

00:04:53.660 --> 00:04:56.596 size:84% position:42%
How can I ask questions
that confront people

00:04:56.596 --> 00:04:57.730 line:92%
but about race and politic

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:58.965 align:start size:94% position:6%
and social-political
structures?"

00:04:58.965 --> 00:05:01.601
So it's like doing Andy but with
a little political bend.

00:05:01.601 --> 00:05:05.972
-When you were a BlackBerr
Pearl-toting college student

00:05:05.972 --> 00:05:07.840 align:start size:94% position:6%
did you know this is
what you wanted to be doing?

00:05:07.840 --> 00:05:09.309 align:start size:94% position:6%
Comedy writing?
-When I took that photo

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:13.112 align:start size:94% position:6%
with you, yes, but I started
college as a math major.

00:05:13.112 --> 00:05:16.916 align:start size:94% position:6%
But then I was, like, a poetry
lover and I loved words.

00:05:16.916 --> 00:05:18.384 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like,
"All poets are very poor.

00:05:18.384 --> 00:05:21.988
How am I going to support my
parents who sacrificed so much

00:05:21.988 --> 00:05:22.689 line:92%
to come to this country?"

00:05:22.689 --> 00:05:24.624 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I did this internship
at Comedy Central.

00:05:24.624 --> 00:05:28.594
It was a rotational progra
that was the Chris Rock interns.

00:05:28.594 --> 00:05:31.397 line:92%
And I fell in love with comedy

00:05:31.397 --> 00:05:32.699 line:92%
I got a joke on "Colbert Report"

00:05:32.699 --> 00:05:34.200 align:start size:94% position:6%
as an intern
that was really chatty.

00:05:34.200 --> 00:05:35.902 align:start size:94% position:6%
And I was like, "Okay, this is
easy. It's great."

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:39.539 align:start size:94% position:6%
And so I went back to Chicago,
did The Onion and then iO,

00:05:39.539 --> 00:05:40.406 line:92%
and a bunch of other stuff

00:05:40.406 --> 00:05:43.176
-Now, when your parents sent you
off to Northwestern

00:05:43.176 --> 00:05:44.844 align:start size:94% position:6%
as a math major,
how did they take the news

00:05:44.844 --> 00:05:47.213
when you went back to them
and said, "Change of plans"?

00:05:47.213 --> 00:05:49.782
-I don't think my parents know
what I do for a living today

00:05:49.782 --> 00:05:52.352 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Even to this day?
-Yes. They're still in denial.

00:05:52.352 --> 00:05:53.152 line:92%
So, ultimately, it's fine.

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.388
-Do they think -- When they hear
you're on the show tonight

00:05:55.388 --> 00:05:58.358 align:start size:94% position:6%
will they assume it's going to
be a math-based interview?

00:05:58.358 --> 00:06:00.693 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Yes, they'll see
lots of equations.

00:06:00.693 --> 00:06:02.228 line:92%
And they'll be like, "Wow, Ziwe,

00:06:02.228 --> 00:06:03.930 align:start size:94% position:6%
you didn't talk about calculus
at all."

00:06:03.930 --> 00:06:06.165 size:75% position:38%
And I don't remember
a damn thing, so...

00:06:06.165 --> 00:06:08.501 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Well, congratulations
on the show.

00:06:08.501 --> 00:06:09.402 align:start size:94% position:6%
-Thank you.
-It is so lovely

00:06:09.402 --> 00:06:12.238 align:start size:94% position:6%
to see you again.
I remember taking that photo -

00:06:12.238 --> 00:06:13.106 line:92%
-Do you really? No, you don't.

00:06:13.106 --> 00:06:14.073 align:start size:94% position:6%
-No, I don't.
-No, you don't.

00:06:14.073 --> 00:06:16.042 align:start size:94% position:6%
[ Laughter ]
-But in the retelling of it,

00:06:16.042 --> 00:06:18.177 size:84% position:42%
because I do like to do
revisionist history,

00:06:18.177 --> 00:06:19.479 align:start size:94% position:6%
I'll say,
"You know, I went back.

00:06:19.479 --> 00:06:20.313 line:92%
I went to this football game

00:06:20.313 --> 00:06:22.849 align:start size:94% position:6%
And there was this one perso
who I thought,

00:06:22.849 --> 00:06:23.649 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
'Sky's the limit.'"

00:06:23.649 --> 00:06:25.752 align:start size:94% position:6%
-And she was screaming,
"Go, Cats!"

00:06:25.752 --> 00:06:26.786 align:start size:94% position:6% line:92%
-Go, Cats!

00:06:26.786 --> 00:06:27.787 align:start size:94% position:6%
Thank you so much
for being here.

00:06:27.787 --> 00:06:30.390 align:start size:94% position:6%
That's Ziwe, everybody.
Her show, "Ziwe," premiere

00:06:30.390 --> 00:06:33.926 size:84% position:42%
this Sunday, May 9th,
at 11 p.m. on Showtime.

